{{/*
  servicedesk.requestDefs — the jq that turns one ZendeskRequest into what the pages show.

  ONE DEFINITION, included by every RESTAction that reads requests: zendesk-requests (the queue)
  and zendesk-request (one request's page) here, and incidents-page's incident-detail ("Zendesk
  requests for this incident"), which carries a BYTE-FOR-BYTE copy of this file. A `define` lives in
  the chart that declares it, so the incident page cannot include it from here, and snowplow's
  shared jq modules are no way round that: a custom module comes from ONE ConfigMap that snowplow's
  own chart renders from its own asset (custom.jq), and a built-in one is embedded in the snowplow
  binary — neither can be shipped by a page chart. So the copy is tested instead:
  test-incident-tickets.py fails if the two files differ, and test-service-desk.py and
  test-incident-tickets.py run the same documented reason table through each. Change both files
  together. Emits defs only (each ends in `;`): put it at the head of a filter.

  THE KIND (zendesk-kog 0.2.1): zendesk.ogen.krateo.io/v2 ZendeskRequest, namespaced.
    spec    configurationRef {name, namespace}, subject, description, priority (low|normal|high|
            urgent), kind (Bug|FeatureRequest), krateo_reference
    status  id (the Zendesk request number), status (new|open|pending|hold|solved|closed),
            priority, url (an API URL), html_url (the end-user page), created_at, updated_at,
            and the Ready and Synced conditions
  url and html_url are DELIBERATELY UNREAD. The requester Zendesk records is the organisation's
  support account, so a person following html_url lands on a request their own Zendesk login cannot
  open. The portal is the window onto the request instead (Diego, 2026-11-13).
  Built from that field list, NOT from a served schema: the CRD is generated by oasgen at the first
  render after the installer pins zendesk-kog, and it was not served on krateo-057 when this was
  written. Verify it against the served schema before relying on an enum here.

  THE STATE IS READ FROM CONDITION STATUS AND REASON, NEVER FROM A MESSAGE. A message is prose for a
  person; its wording changes between provider versions and nothing promises it.

  WHO OWNS THE REASONS: not zendesk-kog. `Available`, `Creating`, `ObserveFailed` and
  `ReconcileError` are provider-runtime's, set by rest-dynamic-controller; `CorrelationTokenMissing`
  is oasgen-provider's `dispatch` verb. So a reason changes with a rest-dynamic-controller or an
  oasgen-provider release, not a zendesk-kog one. The table is documented, with those owners, in
  krateo-blueprints/krateo-zendesk-kog docs/api.md ("Conditions a reader can key on", PR #11,
  measured in the 0.2.0 end-to-end run), and the tests carry it one case per row
  (test-service-desk.py DOCUMENTED_REASONS). Change the table there, then here.

    Ready=True     Available                                   filed       it has a Zendesk number
    Ready=Unknown  ObserveFailed                               unreachable the provider can't read
                                                                           it from Zendesk, most
                                                                           likely an expired token
    Ready=False    Creating, with Synced=False ReconcileError  refused     Zendesk said no
    Ready=False    Creating, otherwise                         filing      not filed yet
    no Ready condition at all                                  filing      the provider hasn't
                                                                           looked at it yet
    Ready=False    CorrelationTokenMissing                     held
    anything else                                              other       the reason VERBATIM,
                                                                           never as progress

  The set of reasons is open. A reason this table does not know is shown as itself, in gray, so a
  new provider failure is visible rather than drawn as "Filing…" forever. That direction is the safe
  one; the other ("anything unknown is still filing") is how a stuck request goes unnoticed.

  THE COLOURS FOLLOW THE STATUS-PILL RULE, as the Ticket queue did. New and Open are slate (a state,
  not a health). Pending, On-hold and "Filing…" are gold, because they are waiting. Solved and
  Closed recede to faint. Nothing is green: a request never asserts health, and the portal's
  indicators are exception-only. "Refused by Zendesk" is red and "Held" orange, because a person has
  to act. These are palette NAMES, resolved per theme by getColorCode.

  THE STATUS WORDS ARE ZENDESK'S, verbatim (New, Open, Pending, On-hold, Solved, Closed): the portal
  names a state as the system that owns it names it. A status value outside the six is shown as
  itself, in gray.
*/}}
{{- define "servicedesk.requestDefs" -}}
def str: if type == "string" then . else "" end;
def obj: if type == "object" then . else {} end;
def zdStatuses: [
  { key: "new", label: "New", color: "slate" },
  { key: "open", label: "Open", color: "slate" },
  { key: "pending", label: "Pending", color: "gold" },
  { key: "hold", label: "On-hold", color: "gold" },
  { key: "solved", label: "Solved", color: "faint" },
  { key: "closed", label: "Closed", color: "faint" } ];
def priorityLabel: str as $p | ({ low: "Low", normal: "Normal", high: "High", urgent: "Urgent" }[$p] // (if $p == "" then "—" else $p end));
def kindLabel: str as $k | ({ Bug: "Bug", FeatureRequest: "Feature request" }[$k] // (if $k == "" then "—" else $k end));
def labelslug: str | ascii_downcase | gsub("[^a-z0-9._-]"; "-") | .[0:63] | sub("^[^a-z0-9]+"; "") | sub("[^a-z0-9]+$"; "");
def condition($t): [ (((.status | obj).conditions // []) | if type == "array" then .[] else empty end) | select(type == "object" and .type == $t) ] | .[0] // null;
def requestView:
  . as $o
  | ($o | condition("Ready")) as $r
  | ($o | condition("Synced")) as $s
  | ($o.status | obj) as $st
  | ($o.spec | obj) as $sp
  | ($o.metadata | obj) as $md
  | ($sp.configurationRef | obj) as $cfg
  | ($st.id | if . == null or . == "" then "" else tostring end) as $id
  | ($st.status | str) as $zd
  | ([ zdStatuses[] | select(.key == $zd) ] | .[0]) as $known
  | (($r // {}).status | str) as $rs
  | (($r // {}).reason | str) as $rr
  | (($s // {}).status | str) as $ss
  | (($s // {}).reason | str) as $sr
  | (if $r == null then "filing"
     elif $rs == "True" and $rr == "Available" then "filed"
     elif $rs == "Unknown" and $rr == "ObserveFailed" then "unreachable"
     elif $rs == "False" and $rr == "Creating" then (if $ss == "False" and $sr == "ReconcileError" then "refused" else "filing" end)
     elif $rs == "False" and $rr == "CorrelationTokenMissing" then "held"
     else "other" end) as $state
  # A Zendesk status is shown only when there is a Zendesk request to have one: filed, or
  # unreachable with a number (then it is the LAST KNOWN status).
  | (($state == "filed" or $state == "unreachable") and $id != "") as $inZendesk
  | (if $inZendesk then
       (if $known != null then { label: $known.label, color: $known.color }
        elif $zd != "" then { label: $zd, color: "gray" }
        else { label: "Filed", color: "slate" } end)
     elif $state == "filed" then { label: "Filed", color: "slate" }
     elif $state == "unreachable" then { label: "Not filed", color: "gray" }
     elif $state == "filing" then { label: "Filing…", color: "gold" }
     elif $state == "refused" then { label: "Refused by Zendesk", color: "red" }
     elif $state == "held" then { label: "Held", color: "orange" }
     else { label: (if $rr != "" then $rr elif $rs != "" then ("Ready=" + $rs) else "Unknown" end), color: "gray" } end) as $pill
  | {
      name: ($md.name | str),
      namespace: ($md.namespace | str),
      subject: ($sp.subject | str),
      description: ($sp.description | str),
      # Zendesk's priority once it has one (an agent may change it), else what was asked.
      priority: (($st.priority | str) as $zp | if $zp != "" then $zp else ($sp.priority | str) end),
      kind: ($sp.kind | str),
      priorityText: ((($st.priority | str) as $zp | if $zp != "" then $zp else ($sp.priority | str) end) | priorityLabel),
      kindText: ($sp.kind | kindLabel),
      id: $id,
      zendeskStatus: (if $inZendesk then $zd else "" end),
      state: $state,
      label: $pill.label,
      color: $pill.color,
      lastKnown: ($state == "unreachable" and $id != ""),
      # The organisation is the configuration the request was filed through, named by its
      # namespace as the raise form names it. A request with no configurationRef (made by hand)
      # falls back to its own namespace, which is where the form always puts it.
      org: { namespace: (($cfg.namespace | str) as $n | if $n != "" then $n else ($md.namespace | str) end), name: ($cfg.name | str) },
      # krateo.io/raised-by is INFORMATIONAL, not a boundary: anyone who may create a request can
      # set it to anything with kubectl. The label is a slug (a label value cannot hold `@`); the
      # annotation, when the form wrote one, is the identity verbatim, so it is what is shown.
      raisedBy: ((($md.annotations | obj)["krateo.io/raised-by"] | str) as $a
                 | if $a != "" then $a else (($md.labels | obj)["krateo.io/raised-by"] | str) end),
      raisedBySlug: (($md.labels | obj)["krateo.io/raised-by"] | str),
      created: ($st.created_at | str),
      updated: ($st.updated_at | str),
      portalCreated: ($md.creationTimestamp | str),
      ready: { status: $rs, reason: $rr, message: (($r // {}).message | str), since: (($r // {}).lastTransitionTime | str) },
      synced: { status: $ss, reason: $sr, message: (($s // {}).message | str) },
      reference: ($sp.krateo_reference | str)
    };
{{- end -}}
